# Puppeteer timelines
@scenario tutorial_lesson_09
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide neutral]
pip: A Puppeteer timeline can move and scale a character. Watch Pip.
[if !tutorial_still]
timeline {
  parallel {
    move "pip" { x:96 y:-12 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
    scale "pip" { sx:1.08 sy:1.08 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
  }
}
[endif]
pip: Open this timeline in Puppeteer. Change the final X position or duration, apply it, and replay.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: Which target moves this character?
> pip -> correct
> bg_current -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Use the character ID to animate Pip. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Use the character ID to animate Pip.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_09]
[flag tutorial_done_09]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_3]
